/-!
# S9-C3h200x: actual Dirac-principal geometry of the P506 spatial profile

The C3h200i coframe profile was generated by the full P506/L0 Lorentz action
before the matter response was recomputed on that profile.  This module
audits the actual Dirac principal needed by that next producer.

The action-generated spatial skew jet has the exact readout

```text
[[0,  1/2, 0, -1/4,  0,    0],
 [-1/2, 0, 0,  0,   -1/4,  0],
 [0,    0, 0,  0,    0,   -1/4]].
```

In the pair order `(01,02,03,23,31,12)`, every spatial derivative axis is
transverse to its own coframe row.  Consequently the matching inverse
coframe row, and hence the matching inverse Dirac gamma, is exactly constant
along all four coordinate axes.  The volume density has zero first derivative
there as well.

These are derived properties of the source/action-generated actual.  No
principal value, inverse row, zero-divergence receipt, target response,
normalization parameter, or branch choice is accepted by a constructor.
-/

namespace
  SaturationMonoid.PhysicsCore.StageNineSourceActionGeneratedP506MatterPreContorsionSpatialProfileDiracPrincipalGeometry

